.TH NORMELOG 1 "octubre 2025" "0.5.1" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
normelog \- Analyzer and filter for norminette with statistics and text/JSON output
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B normelog
[\fIOPTION\fR] [\fIDIRECTORY_OPTION\fR...] [\fIERROR_TYPE\fR...]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B normelog
runs norminette with sane defaults, filters results, computes statistics, and renders them as human text or JSON. It supports directory inclusion/exclusion, respect or ignore of .gitignore, execution from another directory, and optional plugin hooks.
.PP
Internal pipeline:
.RS
.IP \(bu 2
Run norminette with \-R CheckForbidenSourceHeader
.IP \(bu 2
Filter excluded directories from the raw output
.IP \(bu 2
Parse output into FILE/ERR records
.IP \(bu 2
Filter records by error type include/exclude patterns
.IP \(bu 2
Compute statistics (OK/ERR counters, totals per type)
.IP \(bu 2
Format the final result as text or JSON
.RE
.PP
Requirement: \fBnorminette\fR available in the PATH.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Show this manual and exit.
.TP
.BR \-v ", " \-\-version
Show version and exit.
.TP
.B \-a
Show detailed per file error listing (does not change counts, only output).
.TP
.BR \-I ", " \-\-ignore\-gitignore
Do not pass \fB\-\-use\-gitignore\fR when no directories are specified (scan all files, even those ignored by .gitignore).
.TP
.B \-C \fIDIR\fR, \-\-chdir\ \fIDIR\fR, \-\-chdir=\fIDIR\fR
Change working directory to \fIDIR\fR before running. Useful to invoke \fBnormelog\fR from outside the project tree.
.TP
.BR \-d \fIDIR\fR ", " \-d\fIDIR\fR ", " \-\-directory=\fIDIR\fR
Analyze only the provided directories (repeatable).
.TP
.BR \-n \fIDIR\fR ", " \-n\fIDIR\fR ", " \-\-no\-directory=\fIDIR\fR
Exclude directories from the results (repeatable).
.TP
.B \-\-json
Emit JSON output.
.TP
.B \-\-debug
Print debug messages to stderr.
.TP
.B \-\-update
Check for and install the latest version from GitHub releases. Requires curl and appropriate permissions to install.
.TP
.B \-\-no\-update\-check
Disable automatic update check. By default, normelog checks for updates once per day and notifies if a new version is available.
.TP
.B \-\-staged
Check only staged files (git). Useful for pre-commit hooks. Requires a git repository.
.TP
.B \-\-since \fIREF\fR
Check files changed since commit or branch \fIREF\fR. Compares current state with the specified reference. Requires a git repository.
.TP
.B \-\-branch \fIREF\fR
Check files changed in current branch versus base branch \fIREF\fR. Defaults to 'main' if not specified. Requires a git repository.
.TP
.B \-\-watch
Watch mode: continuously monitor files and re-run on changes. Requires either inotifywait (Linux) or fswatch (macOS). Press Ctrl+C to stop.
.TP
.B \-\-severity \fILEVEL\fR
Filter errors by minimum severity level. Valid levels: CRITICAL, WARNING, INFO. Default: INFO (shows all errors).
.TP
.B \-\-max\-errors \fIN\fR
Exit with error code 1 if total error count exceeds \fIN\fR. Useful for CI/CD pipelines with strict quality gates.
.TP
.B \-\-profile \fINAME\fR
Load configuration profile from \fI$XDG_CONFIG_HOME/normelog/profiles/NAME.conf\fR or \fI/etc/normelog/profiles/NAME.conf\fR. Profiles allow maintaining different configurations for different use cases (e.g., strict, dev, ci).
.TP
.B \-\-diff \fIFILE\fR
Compare current run with baseline JSON file and show what errors were fixed or newly introduced. Requires \-\-json output. Exit code 0 if improved or same, 1 if worse.
.TP
.B \-\-save\-baseline \fIFILE\fR
Save current results as baseline JSON file for later comparison with \-\-diff. Requires \-\-json output.
.TP
.B \-\-parallel [\fIJOBS\fR]
Run norminette on multiple files in parallel for faster execution on large codebases. Default: 4 jobs. Requires GNU parallel or xargs with \-P support.
.PP
Error type arguments:
.RS
.IP \(bu 2
One or more patterns to include. Case insensitive substring match.
.IP \(bu 2
Prefix with \- to exclude (for example \-TOO_MANY_VARS_FUNC).
.IP \(bu 2
Include patterns are evaluated before exclude patterns.
.RE
.SH PATTERN FILTERING
Examples:
.RS
.IP \(bu 2
\fBnormelog FORBIDDEN\fR \- show only error types that contain FORBIDDEN.
.IP \(bu 2
\fBnormelog SPACE TAB\fR \- show types containing SPACE or TAB.
.IP \(bu 2
\fBnormelog TOO \-TOO_MANY_VARS_FUNC\fR \- include types with TOO except the excluded one.
.RE
.SH DIRECTORIES
Without \-d/\-\-directory, the current tree is analyzed. By default .gitignore is honored; use \-I to ignore it. With \-d, normelog limits the norminette invocation to the provided directories. \-n performs a post filtering step on resulting records.
.SH OUTPUT
.SS Text
Includes:
.RS
.IP \(bu 2
Summary: Correct files / Incorrect files
.IP \(bu 2
Error type counts
.IP \(bu 2
Detailed listing per file (when \-a or when filtered by type) with type, line, column, and message
.RE
.SS JSON
Approximate schema:
.PP
\fB{ "ok_files": N, "error_files": M, "total_errors": T, "by_type": { TYPE: COUNT, ... }, "files": [ { "file": "path", "errors": [ { "type": "TYPE", "line": L, "col": C, "message": "..." }, ... ] } ] }\fR
.SH STATS
\fBok_files\fR: number of files reported OK. \fBerror_files\fR: files with Error!. \fBby_type\fR: aggregated counts per error type. \fBtotal_errors\fR: total errors after filters.
.SH CONFIG
Loaded if present:
.RS
.IP \(bu 2
/etc/normelog/config
.IP \(bu 2
$XDG_CONFIG_HOME/normelog/config
.RE
These scripts can export variables like \fBNL_OUTPUT\fR or \fBNL_DEBUG\fR.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
\fBNL_OUTPUT\fR
Force output mode (text|json). Default: text.
.TP
\fBNL_DEBUG\fR
Enable debug output (1 enables). Default: 0.
.TP
\fBNL_COLOR\fR
Force color output (1 enables, 0 disables). Default: auto-detected based on whether stdout is a terminal. Set to 0 to disable colors when piping output.
.TP
\fBNL_AUTO_UPDATE_CHECK\fR
Enable or disable automatic update checks (1 enables, 0 disables). Default: 1.
.TP
\fBNL_PARALLEL_JOBS\fR
Number of parallel jobs to use with \fB--parallel\fR. Default: 4. Can also be specified via the \fB--parallel\fR flag argument.
.TP
\fBXDG_CONFIG_HOME\fR
Base directory for user configuration. Default: $HOME/.config. Profile files are searched in $XDG_CONFIG_HOME/normelog/profiles/.
.TP
\fBXDG_CACHE_HOME\fR
Base directory for cache files. Default: $HOME/.cache. Used for storing update check timestamps in $XDG_CACHE_HOME/normelog/.
.SH GIT INTEGRATION
.B normelog
supports incremental checking via git integration, useful for pre-commit hooks and CI/CD pipelines:
.RS
.IP \(bu 2
\fB\-\-staged\fR checks only files staged for commit
.IP \(bu 2
\fB\-\-since HEAD~1\fR checks files changed in the last commit
.IP \(bu 2
\fB\-\-branch main\fR checks files changed in current branch vs main
.RE
.PP
These options filter C and H files only and require a git repository. Helpful error messages suggest alternatives if git is not available.
.SH WATCH MODE
Use \fB\-\-watch\fR to continuously monitor files and re-run normelog on changes. Great for development workflow. Requires:
.RS
.IP \(bu 2
\fBinotifywait\fR on Linux (install with: apt-get install inotify-tools)
.IP \(bu 2
\fBfswatch\fR on macOS (install with: brew install fswatch)
.RE
.PP
Press Ctrl+C to stop watching. The tool clears the screen and shows a timestamp on each run.
.SH SEVERITY LEVELS
Errors are classified into three severity levels:
.RS
.IP \(bu 2
\fBCRITICAL\fR: Forbidden elements, compilation blockers (FORBIDDEN_*, TOO_MANY_FUNCS, etc.)
.IP \(bu 2
\fBWARNING\fR: Code quality and style violations (SPACE_BEFORE_TAB, LINE_TOO_LONG, etc.)
.IP \(bu 2
\fBINFO\fR: Minor formatting issues (EMPTY_LINE_*, TRAILING_WHITESPACE, etc.)
.RE
.PP
Use \fB\-\-severity CRITICAL\fR to show only critical errors, or \fB\-\-severity WARNING\fR to exclude info-level errors. The text output includes a severity breakdown by default.
.SH CONFIGURATION PROFILES
.B normelog
supports configuration profiles for maintaining different settings for different use cases. Create profile files in \fI$XDG_CONFIG_HOME/normelog/profiles/\fR (or \fI/etc/normelog/profiles/\fR for system-wide profiles).
.PP
Example profiles:
.RS
.IP \(bu 2
\fBstrict\fR: No exclusions, fail on any error, show all details. For final code review and submission.
.IP \(bu 2
\fBdev\fR: Exclude minor formatting issues, allow up to 50 errors. For active development.
.IP \(bu 2
\fBci\fR: JSON output, critical errors only, max 10 errors. For CI/CD pipelines.
.RE
.PP
Usage: \fBnormelog --profile strict\fR
.PP
Profile files are sourced as shell scripts and can override any \fBNL_*\fR variables. Example profiles are provided in \fIshare/examples/profiles/\fR.
.SH DIFF MODE
Compare norminette results across code changes to track progress and verify fixes:
.PP
.nf
# Create baseline
normelog --json --save-baseline baseline.json

# After making changes
normelog --json --diff baseline.json
.fi
.PP
The diff output shows:
.RS
.IP \(bu 2
\fBFixed\fR: Errors present in baseline but not in current run
.IP \(bu 2
\fBNew\fR: Errors in current run but not in baseline
.IP \(bu 2
\fBUnchanged\fR: Errors present in both runs
.RE
.PP
Exit code is 0 if the current run is better or equal to the baseline, 1 if worse (more new errors than fixed). Useful in CI to prevent quality regression.
.SH PARALLEL EXECUTION
For large codebases with many files, use \fB\-\-parallel\fR to run norminette on multiple files simultaneously:
.PP
.nf
normelog --parallel      # Use 4 jobs (default)
normelog --parallel 8    # Use 8 jobs
.fi
.PP
Requirements:
.RS
.IP \(bu 2
GNU \fBparallel\fR (preferred): Install with \fBapt-get install parallel\fR or \fBbrew install parallel\fR
.IP \(bu 2
\fBxargs\fR with \fB\-P\fR support (fallback): Usually pre-installed on most systems
.RE
.PP
The tool automatically detects which parallelization method is available. If neither is found, it falls back to sequential execution with a warning.
.PP
Parallel execution is most beneficial for projects with 50+ files. For smaller projects, the overhead may not be worth it.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
0
Successful execution (even if errors were found, unless \-\-max\-errors is exceeded).
.TP
1
Generic execution or parsing error, or \-\-max\-errors threshold exceeded.
.TP
127
\fBnorminette\fR not found on PATH.
.SH COMPLETIONS
Provided files: \fBshare/completion/normelog.bash\fR and \fBshare/completion/_normelog.zsh\fR. \fBmake install\fR will attempt to install them when permissions allow.
.SH PLUGINS
Drop .sh scripts into \fBplugins.d/\fR to extend normelog behavior. Plugins are loaded in alphabetical order at startup.
.PP
Available plugin hooks:
.RS
.IP \(bu 2
\fBnl_hook_pre_norminette()\fR \- Called before norminette execution
.IP \(bu 2
\fBnl_hook_post_parse()\fR \- Called after parsing, can modify records
.IP \(bu 2
\fBnl_hook_post_stats()\fR \- Called after statistics computation
.IP \(bu 2
\fBnl_hook_pre_format()\fR \- Called before formatting output
.RE
.PP
Example plugin:
.nf
#!/usr/bin/env bash
nl_hook_pre_norminette() {
  echo "Running custom pre-checks..."
}
.fi
.SH UPDATE MECHANISM
normelog includes automatic update checking via GitHub Releases. By default, it checks once per 24 hours and notifies when a new version is available. Use \fB--update\fR to manually trigger an update, or \fB--no-update-check\fR to disable the check for a single run. Set \fBNL_AUTO_UPDATE_CHECK=0\fR in your environment or config to permanently disable automatic checks.
.SH EXAMPLES
.nf
# Basic usage
normelog
normelog -a
normelog SPACE TAB
normelog -d src -n build FORBIDDEN
normelog -C ../other-project -I -a
normelog --json INVALID_HEADER LINE_TOO_LONG

# Configuration profiles
normelog --profile strict        # Use strict profile
normelog --profile dev           # Use dev profile

# Diff mode
normelog --json --save-baseline before.json
# ... make changes ...
normelog --json --diff before.json

# Parallel execution
normelog --parallel              # Use 4 jobs
normelog --parallel 8            # Use 8 jobs

# Combined features
normelog --profile ci --parallel 4 --staged
normelog --watch --profile dev
.fi
.SH FILES
.nf
bin/normelog
lib/*.sh
share/completion/normelog.bash
share/completion/_normelog.zsh
share/man/normelog.1
.fi
.SH SEE ALSO
norminette(1)
.SH AUTHOR
normelog project contributors. Reports and patches welcome.
